# Solid Forge — heterogeneous-source (异源) adversarial-review configuration.
# DSH PORT. COPY this file to `.env.solidforge` + fill in what you use (or put the
# vars in your shell / the project `.env`). The wrapper resolves, in
# highest-precedence-first order (setdefault — first-loaded wins, and an
# already-exported shell var always wins):
#   1. <project>/.env.solidforge       — THIS file's live copy (the
#        arm-tools-provisioned Solid Forge secrets file; authoritative for the
#        Solid Forge vars among files).
#   2. <project>/.env                  — the project's generic app env.
#   3. <preset-root>/.env.solidforge   — the DSH SITE DEFAULT: one config covers
#        every project using the solidforge preset (preset root = the directory
#        holding agent.cordis.yml).
#
# This `.env.solidforge.example` is COMMITTED (no real tokens) — provisioned by
# the arm-tools command. The live `.env.solidforge` is gitignored (arm.py adds it).
#
# ── Provider selection (hetero_review.py / hetero_doc_review.py) ─────────────
# Heterogeneity = a DIFFERENT LLM on the SAME harness. The DSH-native DEFAULT is
# worked dsh-substrate profiles (zai-coding-cn.json / minimax-cn.json): the wrapper spawns a fresh, stateless
# `dsh --profile headless` subprocess with a throwaway DSH_HOME pinning the
# route + model. DeepSeek routes are SAME-SOURCE (the DSH orchestrator IS
# DeepSeek) and excluded.
#
#   HETERO_PROFILE=zai-coding-cn,minimax-cn   # comma-list of ARMED profile names; unset = fail-fast arming prompt
#   HETERO_DOC_PROFILE=zai-coding-cn,minimax-cn # csr's separate selector (same rule)
#
# ── Credentials (SHARED-ENV ALIGNMENT 2026-08-25, ADR #54) ───────────────────
# The dsh-substrate profiles declare `_credential_env` pointing at the
# CC-convention vars below (the same vars upstream Claude Code reads by
# convention, and solidforge-pi bridges to its route env via its sf-providers
# extension) — so ONE shared .env.solidforge arms all three harnesses. The dsh
# substrate reads ONLY the `_credential_env` var; the claude-code substrate
# reads ONLY `_token_env` (qwen.json — same var as qwen-token-plan-cn.json:
# one endpoint, one credential, one var).
#
# BIGMODEL_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-your-zhipu-key   # profiles/zai-coding-cn.json (dsh, _credential_env)
# MINIMAX_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-your-minimax-key  # profiles/minimax-cn.json (dsh, _credential_env)
# QWEN_TOKEN_PLAN_CN_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-your-qwen-token-plan-key  # profiles/qwen-token-plan-cn.json (dsh, _credential_env) + profiles/qwen.json (claude-code, _token_env)
#
# Worked examples (armed on the port's own workspace, 2026-08-14) — INSTALLED
# pi-ai CATALOG routes (endpoint + protocol + models inherited; apiKeyEnv only):
#   BIGMODEL_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=<zhipu api key>      profiles/zai-coding-cn.json  model glm-5.2 (reasoning effort supported)
#   MINIMAX_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=<minimax api key>  profiles/minimax-cn.json     model MiniMax-M3 (CN platform key)
#
# ── External-harness opt-in (substrate claude-code; NEVER the default) ───────
# profiles/claude.json (native Claude auth — the CLI's own login, no var) and
# qwen.json ride the Claude Code CLI (a FOREIGN harness kept only for
# Anthropic-compatible-only backends with no pi-ai route). qwen.json reads its
# token via `_token_env` = QWEN_TOKEN_PLAN_CN_ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (same var as
# the dsh qwen-token-plan-cn.json — see above; no separate var needed).
#
# Per-subprocess wall-clock cap (seconds). Default 600; raise for a cold
# large-diff review on the pro tier. Do NOT remap the profile alias to dodge a
# timeout — cold-start is transient, and a global alias remap permanently
# sacrifices review depth on warm calls (ADR #43).
# HETERO_TIMEOUT=1200
